      {
        "text": "And now, these were the thoughts of Ammon, when he saw the afflictions of those whom he termed to be his brethren.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 17:30",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he flattered them by his words, saying: My brethren, be of good cheer and let us go in search of the flocks, and we will gather them together and bring them back unto the place of water; and thus we will preserve the flocks unto the king and he will not slay us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 17:31",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that they went in search of the flocks, and they did follow Ammon, and they rushed forth with much swiftness and did head the flocks of the king, and did gather them together again to the place of water.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 17:32",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "And those men again stood to scatter their flocks; but Ammon said unto his brethren: Encircle the flocks round about that they flee not; and I go and contend with these men who do scatter our flocks.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 17:33",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore, they did as Ammon commanded them, and he went forth and stood to contend with those who stood by the waters of Sebus; and they were in number not a few.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 17:34",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore they did not fear Ammon, for they supposed that one of their men could slay him according to their pleasure, for they knew not that the Lord had promised Mosiah that he would deliver his sons out of their hands; neither did they know anything concerning the Lord; therefore they delighted in the destruction of their brethren; and for this cause they stood to scatter the flocks of the king.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 185,
            "end": 192,
            "text": "Mosiah 28:7; Alma 19:23 (22–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
